WEBVTT

00:10.240 --> 00:12.360
It's a good thing that he's the one coming to us.

00:13.570 --> 00:16.370
Can't we take care of it in there?

00:20.660 --> 00:23.290
We've confirmed phenomena

00:23.290 --> 00:28.170
similar to the Lightless Realm in the
immediate surroundings of the Corpse.

00:29.920 --> 00:34.680
So those who haphazardly
approach it risk losing their minds.

00:34.680 --> 00:36.680
That's what the MA-Vess is for.

00:36.680 --> 00:39.180
But with just a mere prototype...

00:40.890 --> 00:46.270
I also have a report that says that the
suitable pilot is not comfortable boarding it.

00:47.310 --> 00:52.490
Isn't it because you tossed the
Argent in the field as you wished?

00:52.490 --> 00:54.150
Don't you feel accountable for it?

00:54.570 --> 00:59.120
With things as they are, we're forced
to accept the government's demands.

00:59.120 --> 01:04.710
We'll accept one member of the Self-Defense Force in the name of assisting Gargouille.

01:06.830 --> 01:10.250
I'm sure the assistance is in name
only and it's really an internal audit.

01:11.880 --> 01:14.590
I detest her eyes.

01:14.590 --> 01:20.390
In any case, we have a pressing need to
implement the MA-Vess and train its pilot.

01:20.390 --> 01:23.680
The problem now is how we approach things,

01:23.680 --> 01:25.980
since the candidate may refuse boarding the mech.

01:27.980 --> 01:31.020
All is going according to plan.

01:31.020 --> 01:35.570
Their anxiety, their doubts,
their bewilderment, their denial...

01:35.570 --> 01:38.530
...and even their terror!

01:45.040 --> 01:47.210
Hurry up and go!

01:48.170 --> 01:49.960
N-No way!

01:49.960 --> 01:51.840
Just as we practiced.

01:51.840 --> 01:53.130
Come on, let's go.

01:53.130 --> 01:54.210
No!

02:02.010 --> 02:03.640
They're here!

02:03.640 --> 02:07.980
Let's enjoy the best of terrors.

02:11.060 --> 02:16.650
The Dark Metal

02:11.060 --> 02:11.110
The Dark Metal

02:16.650 --> 02:21.070
Night turns to day, and day turns to night. Our wishes have wilted away

02:21.070 --> 02:25.240
Where did the person I want to meet go?

02:25.240 --> 02:29.710
Interlocking these fingers with my beloved

02:29.710 --> 02:33.460
Even though I can't feel them, I continue to live

02:33.500 --> 02:38.090
When the flower's petals

02:38.090 --> 02:42.220
Are plucked off by the wind's playful gale

02:42.220 --> 02:46.680
They are scattered in every direction

02:46.680 --> 02:52.020
Even if you long for it

02:53.020 --> 02:57.740
Don't disappear, just don't

02:57.740 --> 03:01.530
I can even give everything else away if I have to

03:01.530 --> 03:06.370
You were there, and I was there with you

03:06.370 --> 03:10.710
Let me take in these memories

03:10.710 --> 03:17.630
These brief moments are connected, turning it into eternity

03:34.480 --> 03:39.530
Episode 4
Danger, Do Not Mix

03:43.820 --> 03:46.160
The wind carried me pretty far.

03:49.750 --> 03:54.710
This is totally not how I imagined
training on the South Seas would be.

03:54.710 --> 03:59.170
We will now begin the mock
investigation training in uncharted territory.

03:59.550 --> 04:00.630
You have two objectives:

04:01.170 --> 04:06.300
One is to retrieve the transmitter
in the crate that was just dropped,

04:06.720 --> 04:10.060
and the other is for all team
members to gather in one location.

04:12.020 --> 04:16.730
How are we supposed to do that
with no clue to where we landed?

04:16.730 --> 04:18.270
And on a deserted island of all places!

04:18.270 --> 04:21.440
This drill will serve as a stepping stone

04:21.440 --> 04:27.030
for when you start investigating the Lightless Realm, where common sense doesn't apply.

04:27.580 --> 04:30.500
Far better than being forced on the Reaper.

04:30.870 --> 04:36.080
I expect the training objectives will be
met with all eight of you working together,

04:36.080 --> 04:39.710
including Isaku Heito, who landed on the island before you.

04:40.090 --> 04:40.920
That is all.

04:43.470 --> 04:44.680
Heito, really?

04:45.220 --> 04:47.760
With some psychotic murderer?

04:47.760 --> 04:48.930
You've got to be kidding!

04:49.810 --> 04:51.390
This is a deserted island, right?

04:52.230 --> 04:54.480
Wouldn't that make us good prey?

04:56.480 --> 05:01.980
Someone help me... Please!

05:06.450 --> 05:08.370
Isaku Heito.

05:08.370 --> 05:10.240
They said he killed his parents.

05:10.830 --> 05:12.540
What kind of person is he?

05:14.210 --> 05:15.830
A dangerous one.

05:16.500 --> 05:18.290
He's completely off the deep end.

05:18.290 --> 05:19.960
I don't know what he'll do.

05:26.090 --> 05:28.640
Hey! The crate was over there, right?

05:28.970 --> 05:31.100
A parachute came down this way.

05:33.020 --> 05:35.270
That's that girl's...

05:38.730 --> 05:39.770
Honestly...

05:40.610 --> 05:43.480
This is the worst.

05:45.950 --> 05:49.280
Hey, did you feel something special from them?

05:50.200 --> 05:52.740
No, nothing particularly...

05:52.740 --> 05:53.790
You're right.

05:54.250 --> 05:58.370
But there's got to be a reason that they were chosen.

06:00.500 --> 06:03.210
What do you think they're making us do?

06:03.210 --> 06:06.840
Maybe they want us to play tag on a deserted island with a murderer?

06:07.220 --> 06:09.970
If Admonitions are remnants of people's feelings...

06:09.970 --> 06:11.600
You're bringing that up?

06:12.010 --> 06:15.430
Doesn't that make us murderers as well when we defeat Admonitions?

06:20.860 --> 06:21.980
Don't be stupid!

06:22.480 --> 06:24.400
Don't raise your voice.

06:24.400 --> 06:26.280
It'll be bad if Heito hears us.

06:30.660 --> 06:32.200
Something was there just now, right?

06:32.200 --> 06:33.740
Was it him?

06:39.460 --> 06:41.380
Where did Sasame go?

06:44.840 --> 06:46.960
Hey, are you okay?

06:47.720 --> 06:49.800
Are you not feeling well?

06:49.800 --> 06:51.590
Seems that way...

06:51.590 --> 06:53.390
Then wait here.

06:53.390 --> 06:55.890
I'll find the others and bring them back.

06:55.890 --> 06:57.680
Wait! Don't leave me behind!

07:01.060 --> 07:02.730
Don't leave me behind!

07:05.320 --> 07:07.940
What was that just now?

07:12.320 --> 07:13.200
Get on.

07:15.120 --> 07:17.450
I'm not leaving anyone behind.

07:17.450 --> 07:19.410
You're a good guy now?

07:19.410 --> 07:21.120
How fishy.

07:21.120 --> 07:22.830
You want to wait here then?

07:23.830 --> 07:25.210
I'll do it!

07:25.210 --> 07:26.130
I'll get on for you!

07:28.460 --> 07:30.090
Take your hands off my ass.

07:30.090 --> 07:32.430
It's not like I want to.

07:32.430 --> 07:34.100
I'll tell everyone.

07:35.810 --> 07:37.180
You're actually all right, aren't you?

07:37.970 --> 07:40.020
If I was, I'd be walking on my own...

07:42.650 --> 07:45.520
Hey, don't go quiet all of a sudden.

07:45.520 --> 07:47.320
You're always like that.

07:48.610 --> 07:51.200
You're easier to handle when you're like this.

07:52.360 --> 07:54.320
The same goes for you.

08:09.300 --> 08:11.720
What happened to me?

08:27.310 --> 08:28.230
No!

08:34.530 --> 08:36.620
Someone's close by.

08:36.620 --> 08:38.580
But who?

08:42.370 --> 08:45.120
No, I've had enough...

08:45.830 --> 08:47.210
Please...

08:55.890 --> 08:58.930
You can think of this as your home.

08:58.930 --> 09:03.350
We're very happy that you're here with us, Emiru-chan.

09:03.350 --> 09:04.690
You're lying.

09:04.690 --> 09:06.900
You're happy because of the money...

09:04.690 --> 09:06.900
Disaster Security Bond

09:04.690 --> 09:06.900
Type-One Special Disaster • Special Payment Measure #987810

09:07.350 --> 09:11.320
The truth is you find me annoying.

09:11.320 --> 09:12.860
You mock me.

09:12.860 --> 09:16.530
Emiru-chan always smells like an old woman.

09:16.530 --> 09:18.320
Yeah, she's so shabby.

09:19.200 --> 09:23.290
Everyone makes fun of me, but someday I'll...

09:25.410 --> 09:27.170
Hazaki Emiru-san, yes?

09:27.920 --> 09:28.500
Can I help you?

09:28.670 --> 09:31.710
Participant Overviw IX Industrial Department, 3rd Development Section

09:28.670 --> 09:31.710
Lightless Realm New Investigation Plan • Inaugural Special Investigation Team Training Program

09:29.630 --> 09:31.710
May I have a few minutes of your time?

09:34.670 --> 09:39.300
All those crappy, annoying, worthless scrubs...

09:39.300 --> 09:40.850
Right here is where I...

09:44.430 --> 09:46.730
N-No!

09:53.360 --> 09:55.570
Hey, are you all right?

09:55.570 --> 09:56.820
No...

09:56.820 --> 09:58.450
I'm not like that...

09:59.820 --> 10:00.910
No!

10:01.620 --> 10:05.790
I won't! I will never end up looking like that!

10:06.080 --> 10:07.370
What's going on?

10:13.500 --> 10:14.670
Emiru!

10:22.430 --> 10:24.180
AKASHI

10:24.890 --> 10:25.850
This is...

10:27.560 --> 10:27.600
REAPER

10:31.690 --> 10:31.730
AKASHI

10:43.200 --> 10:45.490
Isaku Heito...

11:02.970 --> 11:04.760
Our luggage...

11:04.760 --> 11:05.930
Yeah...

11:06.770 --> 11:08.930
He got the transmitter too.

11:09.730 --> 11:10.690
Heito?

11:10.690 --> 11:11.900
Probably.

11:12.270 --> 11:14.650
He really is on this island.

11:14.650 --> 11:16.360
But where?

11:27.450 --> 11:29.290
So it was you, Sasame.

11:30.830 --> 11:33.250
It felt like you were here.

11:33.710 --> 11:35.000
You can tell?

11:35.000 --> 11:36.840
Yeah, kinda.

11:38.920 --> 11:41.760
I... I can tell too...

11:43.800 --> 11:46.640
Everyone is lost...

11:47.560 --> 11:51.940
They're lost and afraid of something.

11:51.940 --> 11:52.900
Emiru!

11:52.900 --> 11:58.070
I feel the same way... I'm lost too.

12:30.680 --> 12:31.640
I...

12:35.900 --> 12:38.360
You should sing whenever you get anxious.

12:40.360 --> 12:41.320
I will!

12:45.490 --> 12:50.790
Scattered into ashes, here, Garon.

12:52.710 --> 12:57.750
Toss a conch onto the footpath of skulls...

13:00.380 --> 13:01.510
Hey!

13:01.880 --> 13:03.510
Guys!

13:03.510 --> 13:05.130
Over here!

13:10.140 --> 13:12.680
Where's everyone?

13:13.680 --> 13:15.060
Over here!

13:18.480 --> 13:19.650
Was that my imagination?

13:20.650 --> 13:23.240
But if I head over there...

13:25.570 --> 13:27.110
Can I say something strange?

13:27.820 --> 13:28.570
What?

13:29.030 --> 13:32.370
I feel like we'll find everyone if we go that way.

13:34.830 --> 13:36.210
You too, Iwato?

13:38.500 --> 13:39.590
Where?

13:39.590 --> 13:42.050
Where are you?

13:42.050 --> 13:45.470
Hey! We're right here!

13:46.340 --> 13:48.140
Have we met before?

13:48.140 --> 13:50.010
You trying to pick me up?

13:50.010 --> 13:53.390
Nah, that can't be. And, yeah, I feel the same way.

13:54.890 --> 13:57.980
We should go confirm if we're imagining things or not.

13:59.560 --> 14:00.690
Agreed.

14:05.610 --> 14:07.610
Finally found you.

14:07.610 --> 14:09.320
Don't run from me again.

14:10.370 --> 14:13.540
Hey, were you calling the whole time?

14:13.870 --> 14:15.450
It wasn't me.

14:15.450 --> 14:16.790
It's up ahead.

14:18.370 --> 14:19.120
Huh?

14:19.830 --> 14:21.750
Why'd I just think that?

14:22.670 --> 14:24.460
Hey!

14:25.960 --> 14:27.970
Where are you?

14:28.840 --> 14:30.220
We're right here!

14:36.680 --> 14:37.730
You can walk now, right?

14:39.310 --> 14:39.980
Yeah.

14:47.690 --> 14:50.320
Guys!

14:51.410 --> 14:53.490
We're right here!

14:53.950 --> 14:57.870
Where are you guys?

14:59.250 --> 15:00.290
Right here!

15:01.000 --> 15:02.500
We're right here!

15:03.210 --> 15:04.840
Everyone...

15:04.840 --> 15:06.590
Where is everyone?

15:07.800 --> 15:09.880
We're right here!

15:09.880 --> 15:11.390
We're going there now!

15:16.770 --> 15:23.770
One, meddling in affairs of crying children...

15:21.850 --> 15:23.770
They really are here...

15:24.480 --> 15:25.610
This is...

15:25.610 --> 15:34.280
Two, burn the bones of crying children...

15:30.780 --> 15:34.700
I know this song from the past...

15:34.280 --> 15:39.910
Three, atop the carcass is a crying child...

15:36.580 --> 15:38.160
When was the first time...

15:40.040 --> 15:40.710
I heard it?

15:40.710 --> 15:44.670
Quiet, just be quiet, suspicions of the corpses.

15:44.670 --> 15:49.920
Scattered into ashes, here, Garon.

15:59.180 --> 16:00.480
I really found you guys.

16:04.440 --> 16:06.440
Is this for real?

16:06.440 --> 16:08.610
What's happening to us?

16:09.280 --> 16:12.820
We gathered like this in the past.

16:22.160 --> 16:26.290
God, this atmosphere is the worst!

16:26.290 --> 16:27.380
So nauseating...

16:28.710 --> 16:29.960
Heito!

16:32.420 --> 16:35.890
Could it be that the voice guided you as well?

16:35.890 --> 16:38.100
Yeah, that's right.

16:38.100 --> 16:41.020
I heard a voice trembling in terror!

16:42.310 --> 16:44.810
Let me hear more.

16:44.810 --> 16:46.650
So it <i>was</i> you.

16:46.650 --> 16:48.190
Hand that over.

16:49.190 --> 16:50.780
Not happenin'!

16:50.780 --> 16:52.360
It's not enough!

16:52.360 --> 16:55.450
Not enough! Not enough at all!

16:55.450 --> 16:59.910
Not enough terror from you, you, and you!

17:00.830 --> 17:02.870
What the hell is he saying?

17:06.880 --> 17:07.380
Minashi!

17:07.960 --> 17:08.790
Leave it to me!

17:11.170 --> 17:12.090
Look out!

17:16.090 --> 17:17.720
Akashi!

17:17.720 --> 17:19.390
It's just a scratch.

17:19.390 --> 17:20.310
Are you okay?

17:20.310 --> 17:21.970
Yeah. Thanks.

17:22.680 --> 17:24.020
Akashi?

17:33.030 --> 17:35.740
Give me some terror, Akashi!

17:35.740 --> 17:40.660
The best kind of terror, like when I was on the Reaper!

17:41.580 --> 17:43.200
What the hell are you talking about?

17:44.660 --> 17:45.830
I heard.

17:45.830 --> 17:49.210
You're the Reaper master, aren't you?

17:49.210 --> 17:50.290
Come on!

17:51.550 --> 17:53.590
Iwato, restrain him.

17:53.590 --> 17:54.840
Me?

17:54.840 --> 17:56.470
I've got no choice, I guess.

17:56.470 --> 17:58.510
Beats facing an Admonition.

17:58.510 --> 18:00.220
Get up.

18:00.850 --> 18:02.220
Thank you very much.

18:05.600 --> 18:07.140
What?

18:08.600 --> 18:10.400
What is this?

18:12.270 --> 18:14.230
No...

18:14.230 --> 18:17.400
This is not what I was looking for.

18:23.740 --> 18:25.250
Hey, hold on a sec!

18:25.250 --> 18:25.700
Don't.

18:26.250 --> 18:28.210
You'll get lost once the sun sets.

18:28.210 --> 18:30.630
Without him, we can't complete the mission's objective.

18:30.630 --> 18:35.130
The trainer will understand if we explain how crazy he was.

18:35.130 --> 18:38.680
We've already met up once,
so the mission's been accomplished.

18:39.180 --> 18:40.640
That's true.

18:41.050 --> 18:42.220
Are you okay?

18:42.220 --> 18:44.430
We should tend the wound right away.

18:44.430 --> 18:47.230
I'll bring the first-aid kit from the luggage—

18:50.190 --> 18:51.940
It's nothing.

19:02.370 --> 19:03.870
This one isn't done?

19:03.870 --> 19:05.330
No, it's finished.

19:05.620 --> 19:08.370
Iwato, it's gonna burn.

19:08.370 --> 19:09.160
Iwato?

19:10.500 --> 19:17.340
Raika and I weren't the only ones who felt
like we'd meet everyone if we came here, right?

19:21.890 --> 19:25.060
What do you think this power of ours is?

19:25.060 --> 19:28.930
Is it related to us being chosen for the pilot course?

19:28.930 --> 19:30.270
And if it is?

19:30.940 --> 19:36.020
Is that the same reason why the
feelings of Admonitions flow into us?

19:36.020 --> 19:40.900
No... I want to play more.

19:41.950 --> 19:43.570
Play with me.

19:43.950 --> 19:46.540
Admonitions used to be humans.

19:46.910 --> 19:48.910
But they aren't human.

19:48.910 --> 19:50.460
Nothing but their lingering feelings,

19:50.460 --> 19:53.580
regrets, and attachments. It's nothing good.

19:53.580 --> 19:55.540
But that's <i>still</i> human!

19:56.170 --> 19:57.420
Emiru-san...

19:58.710 --> 20:02.970
I also think that feelings are part of a person.

20:02.970 --> 20:05.220
What good does it do to be trapped by the past?

20:10.430 --> 20:16.610
I'm afraid of Admonitions, and of defeating Admonitions.

20:17.070 --> 20:18.690
I feel the same way.

20:18.690 --> 20:21.030
Truth be told, I want to quit all this.

20:30.660 --> 20:31.790
Shooting stars.

20:33.750 --> 20:37.040
Why did we end up like this?

20:37.040 --> 20:37.960
Who knows?

20:48.810 --> 20:51.180
If you want to quit, you can quit.

20:56.560 --> 20:59.570
Though I don't think any of you seriously mean it...

21:02.070 --> 21:03.240
You're right.

21:05.660 --> 21:08.490
The results are going better than I anticipated.

21:08.780 --> 21:14.460
Their powers bloomed as a result of terror, and we found out what their pairings are.

21:15.170 --> 21:16.330
And now...

21:16.960 --> 21:20.210
Who do <i>you</i> want to be friends with?

21:39.770 --> 21:40.230
Who's there?

21:43.240 --> 21:44.320
Heito!

21:47.030 --> 21:48.160
Let me go!

21:49.030 --> 21:50.830
That look of terror.

21:50.830 --> 21:51.870
It's good.

21:51.870 --> 21:52.790
It's great.

21:52.790 --> 21:54.200
Stop it...

21:54.200 --> 21:55.710
Please...

21:56.330 --> 21:59.330
You're trembling so much. What are you afraid of?

21:59.330 --> 22:00.880
Me?

22:00.880 --> 22:02.500
Or maybe...

22:03.670 --> 22:05.970
Let go of me! No!

22:09.840 --> 22:12.140
I finally found you.

22:12.140 --> 22:14.060
You were the one who was calling me.

22:16.350 --> 22:20.060
This has the same flavor of terror as the Reaper.

22:20.900 --> 22:24.360
Oh, this is mine.

22:25.070 --> 22:28.820
You're all mine now.

22:44.800 --> 22:55.430
Throwing away all my excuses, I traced over my abrased heart

22:55.430 --> 22:59.980
In the coldness of the locker room,

22:59.980 --> 23:06.440
Was an unfulfilled promise, locked away

23:06.940 --> 23:12.910
Dispel the darkness in this fallen world,

23:12.910 --> 23:17.450
And give me a reason why I should continue living

23:17.450 --> 23:22.830
The meaning of good-byes, the expectations of people,

23:22.830 --> 23:27.710
And the melodies that we played while never crossing paths

23:27.710 --> 23:33.430
I know I must not run away. The only path is straight ahead

23:33.430 --> 23:37.930
Even if this turns out to be a mistake

23:37.930 --> 23:43.520
The whirlpools of destiny will consume all loneliness

23:43.520 --> 23:51.610
It is an unerasable scar, an egoism that cannot be discarded

24:05.000 --> 24:10.010
Episode 5

24:05.000 --> 24:10.010
Self in Vain
